PZ Mapping Tools - licensing overview
=====================================

PZ Mapping Tools combines and modifies code from Tim Baker's TileZed /
BuildingEd and PZWorldEd source trees. The complete provenance of the source
baseline is recorded in UPSTREAM-HISTORY.md.

The executable editor applications and their GPL-covered source are distributed
under the GNU General Public License version 2, or (where stated by the source
file) any later version. See:

    licenses/GPL-2.0.txt

The libtiled library and tmxviewer contain code under the Simplified BSD
license. See:

    licenses/BSD-2-Clause.txt

The portable Windows build dynamically links against Qt 5.14.2. The Qt
libraries are distributed under the terms described in:

    licenses/Qt-5-LGPL-3.0-GPL-3.0.txt

Other bundled or compiled-in components retain their own licenses and
copyright notices. Their notices and the location of the applicable license
texts are listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt and the licenses directory.

Complete corresponding source for this maintained fork is available at:

    https://github.com/Unjammer/PZ_Mapping_Tools

The unmodified Qt 5.14.2 source archive corresponding to the dynamically linked
Qt runtime is available from:

    https://download.qt.io/archive/qt/5.14/5.14.2/single/

The binary distribution also includes SOURCE-OFFER.txt as a fallback written
offer for the corresponding editor and Qt source.

Project Zomboid game data, Tiles, textures, and other game assets are not part
of this source repository or binary distribution.
